   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Word Roller Typewriter\n\nA sentence with one coloured word that is deleted letter by letter and retyped as the next word, with a block cursor that keeps blinking at the end.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 5 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A tagline whose last word changes (amazing, stunning, powerful), in a typed, code-editor feel.\n- A left-aligned statement on a plain card.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A single line that is only typed once: use typewriter.\n- A swap that should be instant or animated per letter: use a slide or wave roller.\n\nVariables:\n- words (string): Words, default \"amazing, stunning, powerful, seamless\"\n- prefix (string): Prefix, default \"Create something\"\n- font_size (number, 16-200): Font size, default 48\n- color (color): Text color, default \"#0a0a0a\"\n- accent (color): Word color, default \"#2563eb\"\n- cycle_frames (number, 24-120): Frames per word, default 35\n- background (color): Background, default \"#fafafa\"\n- speed (number, 0.25-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
  {
   "path": "scene.html",
   "role": "source",
   "content": "<!doctype html>\n<!--\n  Word Roller Typewriter\n\n  A sentence with one coloured word that is deleted letter by letter and retyped as the next word, with a block cursor that keeps blinking at the end.\n\n  Ported to an HTML + GSAP sub-composition by usemosio/blocks from:\n  https://github.com/lifeprompt-team/remotion-scenes/blob/02c7a84241da7010b5f59c420b0110aafd1d6f0d/src/scenes/RollerAnimations/RollerTypewriter.tsx\n\n  MIT License\n\n  Copyright (c) 2026 lifeprompt-team\n\n  Permission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\n  of this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\n  in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\n  to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\n  copies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\n  furnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\n  The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\n  copies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\n  THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\n  IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\n  FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\n  AUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\n  LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\n  OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\n  SOFTWARE.\n-->\n<html\n  lang=\"en\"\n  data-composition-id=\"word-roller-typewriter\"\n  data-composition-duration=\"5\"\n  data-composition-variables='[\n    {\"id\": \"words\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Words\", \"description\": \"Words in order, separated by commas. The last one is where it settles.\", \"default\": \"amazing, stunning, powerful, seamless\"},\n    {\"id\": \"prefix\", \"type\": \"string\", \"role\": \"content\", \"label\": \"Prefix\", \"description\": \"Fixed text before the typed word.\", \"default\": \"Create something\"},\n    {\"id\": \"font_size\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Font size\", \"description\": \"Size of the text in pixels. A wide line shrinks to fit the frame.\", \"default\": 48, \"min\": 16, \"max\": 200, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"px\"},\n    {\"id\": \"color\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Text color\", \"description\": \"Color of the fixed text.\", \"default\": \"#0a0a0a\"},\n    {\"id\": \"accent\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Word color\", \"description\": \"Color of the typed word and the cursor.\", \"default\": \"#2563eb\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cycle_frames\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Frames per word\", \"description\": \"How long each word is shown, in 30 fps frames.\", \"default\": 35, \"min\": 24, \"max\": 120, \"step\": 1, \"unit\": \"f\"},\n    {\"id\": \"background\", \"type\": \"color\", \"role\": \"style\", \"label\": \"Background\", \"description\": \"Fill behind the text. Use transparent to lay the block over your own footage.\", \"default\": \"#fafafa\"},\n    {\"id\": \"speed\", \"type\": \"number\", \"role\": \"motion\", \"label\": \"Speed\", \"description\": \"Playback speed multiplier.\", \"default\": 1, \"min\": 0.25, \"max\": 4, \"step\": 0.05, \"unit\": \"x\"}\n  ]'\n>\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <title>Word Roller Typewriter</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <template>\n      <link\n        rel=\"stylesheet\"\n        href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Geist:wght@100;300;400;500;600;700;800;900&amp;display=block\"\n      />\n      <style>\n        #root {\n          position: absolute;\n          inset: 0;\n          overflow: hidden;\n          container-type: size;\n          font-family: var(--font-display, Geist, system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif);\n          pointer-events: none;\n        }\n        .wty-stage { position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }\n\n        #root { color: var(--c, #0a0a0a); }\n        .wty-stage { justify-content: flex-start; padding: 0 5.2%; }\n        .wty-g { line-height: 1.2; white-space: pre; position: relative; font-weight: 500; }\n        .wty-w { color: var(--ac, #2563eb); }\n        .wty-cur { display: inline-block; width: 0.0625em; height: 1em; background: var(--ac, #2563eb); margin-left: 0.04em; vertical-align: middle; }\n\n      </style>\n\n      <div id=\"root\" data-composition-id=\"word-roller-typewriter\" data-duration=\"5\" data-fps=\"30\">\n        <div id=\"wty-clip\" class=\"wty-stage clip\" data-start=\"0\" data-duration=\"5\" data-track-index=\"0\">\n          <div id=\"wty-g\" class=\"wty-g\"><span id=\"wty-pre\"></span> <span class=\"wty-w\"><span id=\"wty-t\"></span><span id=\"wty-cur\" class=\"wty-cur\"></span></span></div>\n        </div>\n\n        <script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/gsap@3.14.2/dist/gsap.min.js\"></script>\n        <script>\n          (function () {\n            \"use strict\";\n\n            var root = document.getElementById(\"root\");\n            var vars =\n              window.__hyperframes && window.__hyperframes.getVariables\n                ? window.__hyperframes.getVariables()\n                : {};\n            function el(id) { return document.getElementById(id); }\n            function num(value, fallback, min, max) {\n              var n = Number(value);\n              return value !== \"\" && value !== null && value !== undefined && Number.isFinite(n) ? Math.min(max, Math.max(min, n)) : fallback;\n            }\n            function str(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" && value.trim() ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function txt(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"string\" ? value : fallback;\n            }\n            function bool(value, fallback) {\n              return typeof value === \"boolean\" ? value : value === \"true\" ? true : value === \"false\" ? false : fallback;\n            }\n            function list(value, fallback, max) {\n              var a = (typeof value === \"string\" ? value : \"\").split(\",\").map(function (s) { return s.trim(); }).filter(Boolean);\n              if (!a.length) a = fallback.slice();\n              return a.slice(0, max || 12);\n            }\n            function bezier(x1, y1, x2, y2) {\n              return function (x) {\n                if (x <= 0) return 0;\n                if (x >= 1) return 1;\n                var lo = 0, hi = 1, t = x;\n                for (var i = 0; i < 32; i++) {\n                  var u = 1 - t;\n                  var cx = 3 * u * u * t * x1 + 3 * u * t * t * x2 + t * t * t;\n                  if (cx < x) lo = t; else hi = t;\n                  t = (lo + hi) / 2;\n                }\n                var v = 1 - t;\n                return 3 * v * v * t * y1 + 3 * v * t * t * y2 + t * t * t;\n              };\n            }\n            var E = {\n              out: bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), \"in\": bezier(0.7, 0, 0.84, 0), inOut: bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1),\n              overshoot: bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1), smooth: bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1),\n              quadIn: function (x) { return x * x; },\n              quadOut: function (x) { return 1 - (1 - x) * (1 - x); },\n              cubicOut: function (x) { return 1 - Math.pow(1 - x, 3); },\n              cubicInOut: function (x) { return x < 0.5 ? 4 * x * x * x : 1 - Math.pow(-2 * x + 2, 3) / 2; }\n            };\n            function clamp01(p) { return Math.min(1, Math.max(0, p)); }\n            // the source framework interpolate with clamped ends, one input range and one output range.\n            function ip(x, a, b, from, to, ease) {\n              var p = b === a ? (x >= b ? 1 : 0) : clamp01((x - a) / (b - a));\n              return from + (to - from) * (ease ? ease(p) : p);\n            }\n            // Damped spring from 0 towards 1 (mass, stiffness, damping), frame at 30 fps, in closed form.\n            function spring(frame, cfg) {\n              if (frame <= 0) return 0;\n              var t = frame / 30, m = cfg.mass || 1, k = cfg.stiffness === undefined ? 100 : cfg.stiffness, c = cfg.damping === undefined ? 10 : cfg.damping;\n              var w0 = Math.sqrt(k / m), z = c / (2 * Math.sqrt(k * m));\n              if (Math.abs(z - 1) < 1e-6) return 1 - Math.exp(-w0 * t) * (1 + w0 * t);\n              if (z < 1) {\n                var wd = w0 * Math.sqrt(1 - z * z);\n                return 1 - Math.exp(-z * w0 * t) * (Math.cos(wd * t) + (z * w0 / wd) * Math.sin(wd * t));\n              }\n              var q = w0 * Math.sqrt(z * z - 1), r1 = -z * w0 + q, r2 = -z * w0 - q;\n              return 1 - (r2 * Math.exp(r1 * t) - r1 * Math.exp(r2 * t)) / (r2 - r1);\n            }\n            // Seeded generator (mulberry32).\n            function rng(seed) {\n              var a = seed >>> 0;\n              return function () {\n                a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n                var t = a;\n                t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n                t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n                return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n              };\n            }\n            function onFonts(fn) {\n              if (document.fonts && document.fonts.ready) document.fonts.ready.then(fn, function () {});\n            }\n            // Sets the group's font size, then shrinks it so the group (or its probe) fits the frame.\n            function fitG(g, size, probe, wf, hf, wmul) {\n              g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\";\n              var p = probe || g;\n              var w = Math.max(1, p.offsetWidth * (wmul || 1)), h = Math.max(1, p.offsetHeight);\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * (wf || 0.9) / w, root.clientHeight * (hf || 0.9) / h);\n              if (k < 1) { size = Math.max(6, size * k); g.style.fontSize = size + \"px\"; }\n              return size;\n            }\n            function fillSizer(sizer, words) {\n              sizer.textContent = \"\";\n              words.forEach(function (w) {\n                var s = document.createElement(\"span\");\n                s.textContent = w;\n                sizer.appendChild(s);\n              });\n            }\n            function setText(node, value) {\n              if (node.__t !== value) { node.__t = value; node.textContent = value; }\n            }\n            var speed = num(vars.speed, 1, 0.25, 4);\n            var TOTAL = parseFloat(root.dataset.duration || \"5\");\n            var clock = { frame: 0 };\n            function start(draw) {\n              var tl = gsap.timeline({ paused: true });\n              tl.to(clock, { frame: Math.round(TOTAL * 30), duration: TOTAL, ease: \"none\", onUpdate: function () { draw(Math.round(clock.frame * speed * 1000) / 1000); } }, 0);\n              draw(0);\n              tl.seek(0);\n              window.__timelines = window.__timelines || {};\n              window.__timelines[\"word-roller-typewriter\"] = tl;\n            }\n\n            root.style.background = str(vars.background, \"#fafafa\");\n            \n            var words = list(vars.words, [\"amazing\", \"stunning\", \"powerful\", \"seamless\"], 10);\n            var fi = words.length - 1;\n            var cd = num(vars.cycle_frames, 35, 24, 120);\n            var g = el(\"wty-g\"), pre = el(\"wty-pre\"), t = el(\"wty-t\"), cur = el(\"wty-cur\");\n            if (typeof vars.color === \"string\" && vars.color) root.style.setProperty(\"--c\", vars.color);\n            if (typeof vars.accent === \"string\" && vars.accent) root.style.setProperty(\"--ac\", vars.accent);\n            pre.textContent = txt(vars.prefix, \"Create something\");\n            var longest = words.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return b.length - a.length; })[0];\n            var probe = document.createElement(\"div\");\n            probe.style.cssText = \"position:absolute;visibility:hidden;white-space:pre;left:0;top:0\";\n            probe.textContent = pre.textContent + \" \" + longest;\n            g.appendChild(probe);\n            var base = num(vars.font_size, 48, 16, 200);\n            function fit() {\n              g.style.fontSize = base + \"px\";\n              var k = Math.min(1, root.clientWidth * 0.84 / Math.max(1, probe.offsetWidth * 1.03));\n              if (k < 1) g.style.fontSize = Math.max(6, base * k) + \"px\";\n            }\n            fit();\n            onFonts(fit);\n\n            // remocn-scenes: 12 frames deleting the previous word at 1.2 letters a frame, a pause,\n            // typing from frame 15 at 0.8 letters a frame; the last word stays with a blinking cursor.\n            function draw(f) {\n              var ci = Math.min(Math.floor(f / cd), fi);\n              var word = words[ci];\n              var cT = ci >= fi ? cd : f % cd;\n              var shown = \"\", showCursor = true, ff = Math.floor(f);\n              if (ci >= fi) {\n                shown = word;\n                showCursor = Math.floor(ff / 15) % 2 === 0;\n              } else if (cT < 12) {\n                var prev = words[Math.max(0, ci - 1)];\n                shown = prev.slice(0, Math.max(0, prev.length - Math.floor(cT * 1.2)));\n              } else if (cT >= 15) {\n                var typed = Math.min(word.length, Math.floor((cT - 15) * 0.8));\n                shown = word.slice(0, typed);\n                showCursor = typed < word.length || Math.floor(ff / 8) % 2 === 0;\n              }\n              setText(t, shown);\n              cur.style.visibility = showCursor ? \"visible\" : \"hidden\";\n            }\n            start(draw);\n\n          })();\n        </script>\n      </div>\n    </template>\n  </body>\n</html>\n"
  }
 ],
